## Delivered

- Complete deterministic accountant/client intake workflows behind the frozen
  T01 public signatures: server-scoped 2025 case/checklist creation, one-time
  links, revocable sessions, adaptive questions, immutable answers/documents/
  attempts/submissions/audits, upload validation and duplicate cleanup,
  progress/readiness replay through TaxCases, and exact immutable review
  association.
- Persistence references exactly ClientIntake, TaxCases, and Tenancy,
  implements the scoped SQL store, and adds only the twelve intake metadata
  tables in migration 20260730000000_AddClientIntake. The initial migration and
  every existing review/identity table are unchanged.
- The portal references ClientIntake, validates all intake configuration,
  supplies CSPRNG credentials and purpose-separated keyed digests, and registers
  a versioned AES-GCM streaming content adapter only in Development/test.
- The content port remains write-only. SQL stores no filename or source bytes;
  opaque source objects are outside web root, authenticated and encrypted, and
  scoped fingerprints are non-correlatable across firms/cases.
- Active guidance records the implemented-but-not-HTTP-exposed backend and exact
  dependency/schema/content boundaries.

## Human-authorized unblock amendments

The human explicitly authorized the changes needed to unblock T02 after the
inherited Claude work:

1. `tests/Persistence.Tests/Support/RelationalTestContext.cs` and
   `tests/Persistence.Tests/Repositories/ReviewRecordVersioningTests.cs` now
   apply all migrations and permit the SQLite provider's pending-model warning.
   Additive migration T02 made the prior initial-migration-only harness stale.
2. `tests/Persistence.Tests/Upgrade/EfUpgradeBaselineTests.cs` continues to
   freeze the original EF baseline while filtering T02's exact additive intake
   entities/tables/migration from that historical comparison.
3. `tests/TaxAI.Portal.Tests/Upgrade/UpgradeBaselineContractTests.cs` admits only
   T02's exact additive reference/type set while retaining every earlier
   baseline assertion.
4. `tests/TaxAI.Portal.Tests/Identity/CookieAndTokenTests.cs` no longer scans the
   randomly generated opaque session GUID for a nine-digit taxpayer pattern.
   The protected cookie payload and every actual taxpayer/PII exclusion remain
   asserted.
5. The task's planned filename `CryptographicIntakeSecretSource.cs` conflicts
   with the repository-wide tracked-filename hygiene rule. The implementation
   is `CryptographicIntakeCredentialSource.cs`, matching T01's already-amended
   `IIntakeCredentialSource` port. No hygiene assertion was weakened.

## Deliberately not shipped

No intake HTTP route, upload transport, intake component, Interactive Server,
raw-content preview/download, extraction, parsing, tax processing, review
construction, production content provider, retention/purge path, deployment,
merge, or self-approval.

